    {
      "section": "time.clock",
      "confidence": "low",
      "note": "Best effort per orchestrator instruction. Additive 'awola {h}' (awola = hour/time, Bulu-Fang-Ewondo loan from 'hora') and 'awola {h} ai minit N' (ai = and/with; minit = minute loan). Minute numerals use the Fang tens pattern mewom + agreeing numeral (mewom mebú 20, mewom melaa 30, mewom menyin 40, mewom metán 50) with 'ai tán' for the fives, spelled to match the existing hours list ('awom mebú', 'aláa'). Specific doubts: (1) whether speakers say 'awola bè' or a plural 'mewola mebè' for hours >1; (2) 'minit' vs another loan or native word; (3) no half-word used, :30 is 'thirty minutes'; (4) the existing hours list itself is suspect ('abúi' normally means 'many'; Fang 2 is 'bɛ̀/bè') and was left untouched. Needs a Fang speaker's review."
    }
  ]
